# GitHub Actions runners are Linux, and these workflows embed shell scripts.
# A carriage return at end of line breaks heredoc terminators there (the
# closing token never matches) and it breaks on the runner rather than here,
# which is the expensive kind of failure.
#
# core.autocrlf=true already normalizes these to LF on this machine, so this is
# belt and braces, not a fix for an observed bug. It is worth pinning anyway:
# autocrlf is per-machine config, so a clone on a box with autocrlf=false would
# behave differently and nothing in the repo would say so.
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
